From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:59:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: add a ramoops region

The first T8132 sleeps on a J604 ended in a watchdog reset with nothing
of the kernel's log on disk past the start of the suspend, and no
pstore region existed to keep it.

Reserve 1 MiB for ramoops in the middle of the J604's one large piece
of RAM, well clear of the boot loader's low and top carveouts as a
running J604 reports them: oops and panic records, and with the pstore
console the console too, for the next boot to read, if DRAM keeps its
contents through the reset.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 41890533c2..514d38afe5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1661,3 +1661,21 @@ &mtp {
 &mtp_hid {
 	iommus = <&mtp_dart 1>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * A pstore region for bring-up: what the kernel logs can outlast a watchdog
+ * reset there, if DRAM keeps its contents through the reset (to be shown by
+ * the first one). 1 MiB in the middle of the J604's one large piece of RAM,
+ * well clear of the boot loader's low and top carveouts (26B123 memory map,
+ * read on a running J604). Records oops and panic dumps; with the pstore
+ * console it also keeps the console.
+ */
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	ramoops@10200000000 {
+		compatible = "ramoops";
+		reg = <0x102 0x00000000 0x0 0x100000>;
+		record-size = <0x20000>;
+		console-size = <0x80000>;
+		pmsg-size = <0x0>;
+	};
+};
-- 
